  {
   "_id": 11426,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"7767\" data-start=\"7642\">Paradigm choice affects scalability, modularity, and code clarity. For example, in a Library Management System:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"7932\" data-start=\"7768\">\n\t<li data-end=\"7833\" data-start=\"7768\">\n\t<p data-end=\"7833\" data-start=\"7770\"><strong data-end=\"7777\" data-start=\"7770\">OOP</strong> helps in defining classes for Book, Member, Transaction</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"7878\" data-start=\"7834\">\n\t<p data-end=\"7878\" data-start=\"7836\"><strong data-end=\"7852\" data-start=\"7836\">Event-driven</strong> supports UI interactivity</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"7932\" data-start=\"7879\">\n\t<p data-end=\"7932\" data-start=\"7881\"><strong data-end=\"7895\" data-start=\"7881\">Procedural</strong> handles reports and batch operations</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"7944\" data-start=\"7934\">Using OOP:</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"7944\" data-start=\"7934\">class Book:<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; def __init__(self, title, author):<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.title = title<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.author = author<br />\nParadigm selection depends on use-case complexity. Evaluating this ensures long-term maintainability and cleaner design.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 5,
